cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the preprint, please cite it as below."
title: "从意义权到认知沉积：PACSP-ID 框架的理论建构、创新动力学标识与验证工程"
abstract: >-
  PACSP-ID (Pan-Agent Cognitive Sediment Protocol — Identity) measures cognitive
  deposition along an agent's trajectory. The core quantity is the
  Lebesgue-Stieltjes integral C_T = ∫ μ dΛ, in units of Se (瑟), where μ is the
  Fisher-information cognitive curvature and Λ the total-variation path measure.
  The framework couples a philosophy of meaning-rights, an emotion-tree extension,
  and an innovation-dynamics layer, with six-layer cryptographic attestation.
  This version reports measured results on three content domains (poetry, lyrics,
  technical documents, 31 items each) and three negative results that are recorded
  rather than tuned away.
